{"title":"2003 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is made up of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> squares, each with side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The area of the square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />, in square units, is\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/99605ba216edbde062b6b73f77cbe2c2df8a9ecd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 12 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 16 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 18 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the side lengths of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Square\" title=\"Square\">square</a> are all equal to each other, we only need to find one of the side lengths of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>The angles of squares are also all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7dfa8a2a90d521b2b03f5b82a1fb9f85dce88c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^{\\circ}$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" />, so we know that triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/7/e57c20f8accaa47e01b7a64ed7b7b39e1e645b69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KBL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right triangle</a>, which means that we can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Pythagorean theorem\">pythagorean theorem</a>.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5353006e331ae7627ba70b74800faad67aba902b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KB = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"67\" height=\"14\" />, since the side lengths of the tiny squares are all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Using this logic, we also get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86af73aec492828657ac6cec0e882529846ab9bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BL = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Using the pythagorean theorem, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/e/02e329e5e13e95b2199e918faed918ede8c033c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KB^2 + BL^2 = KL^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/b/16b9fff793fc7f43b60629e408e97903c5402876.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4^2 + 2^2 = KL^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02d72c10dc55b5f19eb68ba706e3d4a7a414189a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL^2 = 16 + 4 = 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef091d889893c7c10e475a93e4ef626ff70aa5ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is one of the side lengths of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />, and the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Area\" title=\"Area\">area</a> of a square is the square of its side length. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f97d59bfd77e0eb17be6f8e2e0fe9bc1bf9459f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL^2 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"128\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To find the area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8baa210c35a8d98d01f9f4d4c956c5a7bcd15ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KLMN$\" width=\"65\" height=\"12\" />, we can subtract the area of the triangles from the total area.\n</p><p>Since the angles of a square are all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Right angles\">right angles</a>, we know that the triangles are all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Right triangles\">right triangles</a>.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>We can also see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9883f11fa61c163f140f0caa1f102e6d6a6449.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN = KB = MD = CL = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"231\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92f3cc70c283c1a87eb6b800a0cf914671ee75a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AK = BL = CM = ND = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"231\" height=\"14\" /> using the same logic found in solution 1.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Because the legs of the triangles are equal to each other, the areas are the same, and we only need to find one of the areas. We can multiply this area by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to get the total area of the triangles:\n</p><p>The area of a triangle is its height multiplied by one of its sides, which is the length of the legs multiplied together in a right triangle, divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca1872899a84a1db01f87d91290f1b8722690cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2 \\times 4}{2} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"80\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying this by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/1/541f4f0ac5c46d4e572ab6d69e704f8ad1810583.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\times 4 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>We can now find the total area of square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. Since a square's area is its side length squared, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/2/242bade7eecb8dbe7d1ef62e8008cfb581dbe77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6^2 = 36$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Subtracting the total area of the triangles from the total area of the square, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d733d6ea97452c9edb2f75082c527ecad0c439a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 - 16 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(D) } 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"150\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202401\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.037 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 150/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1517/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4950/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.512      1 -total\n 66.12%    5.628      5 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:32623:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202401 and revision id 251794. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}